-- title:
--   Division by Xᵢ - bᵢ over a J-adically complete ring
-- statement:
--   Let $E$ be a commutative ring and $J \subseteq E$ an ideal such that $E$ is $J$-adically complete, i.e. the $J$-adic filtration is both separated (the intersection of the ideals $J^n$ is zero, in the `IsHausdorff` sense) and precomplete (every sequence that is Cauchy for the $J$-adic filtration has a limit). Let $d$ be a natural number and let $b : \mathrm{Fin}\, d \to E$ be a $d$-tuple of elements of $E$, each lying in the radical of $J$, that is, for every $i$ some power of $b_i$ belongs to $J$. Let $c$ be an arbitrary formal power series in the variables indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\, d$ with coefficients in $E$. The assertion is that there exist a constant $r \in E$ and power series $q_i \in E[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]$, indexed by $i \in \mathrm{Fin}\, d$, such that
--   $$c \;=\; \mathrm{C}(r) + \sum_{i} (X_i - \mathrm{C}(b_i))\, q_i,$$
--   where $\mathrm{C}$ denotes the inclusion of constants into the multivariate power series ring and $X_i$ the $i$-th variable. No uniqueness of $r$ or of the $q_i$ is claimed.
--
--   This is a division-with-remainder (Weierstrass-type) statement: every power series over a $J$-adically complete ring is congruent to a constant modulo the ideal generated by $X_1 - b_1, \dots, X_d - b_d$, provided the $b_i$ are topologically nilpotent in the sense of lying in the radical of $J$; consequently evaluation at $b$ identifies $E[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]/(X_i - b_i)$ with $E$, even though the substitution $X \mapsto X + b$ makes no sense formally. It is used in the study of formal groups over complete rings, namely for [`FormalGroup.IsDrinfeldBasisAdic.map_iso`](thm.html#FormalGroup.IsDrinfeldBasisAdic.map_iso) and for the computation of the quotients of a power series ring by the ideals generated by the components of $[p^v]$ shifted by a point.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvPowerSeries_exists_C_add_sum_X_sub_C_mul_of_mem_radical_of_isAdicComplete.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open MvPowerSeries

universe u

theorem MvPowerSeries.exists_C_add_sum_X_sub_C_mul_of_mem_radical_of_isAdicComplete
    {E : Type u} [CommRing E] (J : Ideal E) [IsAdicComplete J E]
    {d : ℕ} (b : Fin d → E) (hb : ∀ i, b i ∈ J.radical) (c : MvPowerSeries (Fin d) E) :
    ∃ (r : E) (q : Fin d → MvPowerSeries (Fin d) E),
      c = MvPowerSeries.C r + ∑ i, (MvPowerSeries.X i - MvPowerSeries.C (b i)) * q i := by sorry
